# Tailwind-Only Styling

Use Tailwind CSS utility classnames for all styling. Do not write custom CSS or inline styles.

## Required

- Style elements with `className` and Tailwind utilities
- Prefer composing utilities over custom CSS
- Extract repeated class patterns into components, not CSS classes

## Forbidden

- New `.css` / `.scss` / `.module.css` files (except Tailwind entry / config)
- Inline `style={{ ... }}` props (except dynamic values Tailwind cannot express)
- Custom selectors, hand-written properties, or CSS-in-JS for layout/visual styling

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<div style={{ marginTop: 16, color: 'red' }} />
// custom.css: .card { padding: 1rem; }

// ✅ GOOD
<div className="mt-4 text-red-500" />
<div className="p-4" />
```

When a value must be dynamic (e.g. computed pixel position), prefer a Tailwind arbitrary value (`w-[var(--x)]`) or a minimal inline style only for that dynamic property—still use Tailwind for everything else.
